.TH INVF-RESIZE 8 "2026-09" "InvariantFS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
invf-resize \- grow or shrink an InvariantFS volume offline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B invf-resize
.IR image | device
.IR newsize [ K | M | G ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B invf-resize
resizes an InvariantFS volume (WP18). The volume must be unmounted.
.I newsize
is a byte count with an optional K/M/G suffix and is rounded down to a
whole block; the minimum volume size is 64 MiB.
.PP
The resize is staged as an RSZ0 record and rolled forward idempotently at
the next volume open, so an interrupted resize simply continues.
.PP
For two-device (WP25) volumes
.I newsize
is the total across both devices; growth lands on the tail device (dev1,
named by the
.B INVFS_DEV1
environment variable or the hint recorded at mkfs time). Shrinking a
two-device volume is refused.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INVFS_DEV1
Path of the second device of a two-device volume.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on errors (too-small target, I/O failure, refusal); 2 on
usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR invf-mkfs (8),
.BR invarifs (7)
